{"actions":[{"date":"2026-03-26","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Agriculture.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-03-26","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-03-26","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[],"total":0},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2026-03-26","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsag00","name":"Agriculture Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":16,"fetched_at":"2026-10-26T07:56:34+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":45,"viability":25.0}],"id":"119-hr-8104","importance":45,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":46.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Directly affects fertilizer manufacturers, wholesalers, farmers, and market participants who interact with the new reporting and survey programs.","evidence":"The corporate officers or officially designated representatives of each manufacturer or wholesaler of nitrogen, phosphorous, or potassium for use as fertilizer shall report to the Secretary at least weekly","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":50},{"assessment":"Imposes mandatory weekly reporting requirements on manufacturers and wholesalers and establishes survey and data publication duties for the Department of Agriculture.","evidence":"The Secretary shall establish a program of fertilizer and fertilizer product price information reporting","evidence_verified":true,"key":"magnitude","score":40},{"assessment":"Requires the Secretary of Agriculture to establish reporting programs, conduct weekly retail surveys, and summarize data on a dashboard, though specific dollar amounts for appropriations are not stated.","evidence":"The Secretary shall establish a program within Market News of the Agricultural Marketing Service--to conduct not less frequently than weekly surveys of retail fertilizer prices","evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":30},{"assessment":"Amends the Agricultural Marketing Act of 1946 to add a new mandatory price reporting section, regular reviews, and potential future rulemaking by the Secretary.","evidence":"To amend the Agricultural Marketing Act of 1946 to establish a mandatory price reporting program for fertilizer","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":50},{"assessment":"Establishes permanent ongoing weekly reporting, data summaries, and biennial reviews by the Secretary of Agriculture.","evidence":"Not less frequently than once every 2 years, the Secretary shall review the information required to be reported","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":60}],"missing_information":["Specific figures on federal appropriations or costs required to implement the program.","Exact number of businesses or individuals that will be mandated to report versus those exempt."],"rationale":"The bill establishes a mandatory price reporting program for fertilizer manufacturers and wholesalers, as well as weekly retail surveys and data summaries by the Secretary of Agriculture. It directly affects fertilizer manufacturers, wholesalers, and market participants while exempting cooperatives and non-manufacturer retailers from mandatory reporting. The changes are regulatory and administrative within the agricultural sector, lasting indefinitely.","score":45},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T12:44:01+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr8104/BILLS-119hr8104ih.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2026-03-26","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 8104","latest_action":{"date":"2026-03-26","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Agriculture."},"members":[{"chamber":"House","district":"At Large","id":"J000301","name":"Rep. Johnson, Dusty","party":"R","role":"sponsor","state":"SD"}